Converting between JIM .ROI and NIFTI volumetric binary mask

-Save ROI segmented file as .roi.
-Load original nifti in JIM9.
-Go into main JIM window, go to Process>Masker
	-in the File field, enter the image file name for the image to be masked
	-Click mask outside to retain the inner volume of the ROI, or mask 	inside to set the enclosed region to 0. 
	-Pick the ROI file where it asks for the ROI file
	-Combination mode union https://www.xinapse.com/Manual/masking/
	-Pixel area threshold 50%
	-Save settings>apply
	-When the bottom left says masking complete save the result as a new image

